From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 14:11:33 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 221/342] dwc2: high speed isochronous IN at any service
 interval, two streams

High speed isochronous endpoints with bInterval 2 to 16 (a packet every
2^(bInterval-1) microframes, as a webcam's microphone has, 4: once a
millisecond): a packet at most two microframes away is armed from the
halt of the one before, a later one by the timer in the microframe
before its own. A stream that falls behind goes on from the next
microframe and counts the ones it missed. A second high speed stream
(channels 4 and 5), so a webcam's video and microphone run together.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
